Day 1 — Backend:
    ✔ 1. One small branch + PR per step, merged straight into main (= deploy; decided 11-8-26, CLAUDE.md "How it ships"): store closed by default hides unfinished work; backup before PRs with new models; tell Impact the app may restart often; back to the timing rule if the shop takes orders again — PR #20 (docs + DNS_SERVERS) merged; this step on feat/storefront-models @done(26-11-08)
    ✔ 2. Models (branch feat/storefront-models; nothing requires them yet, so no effect on the running app) @done(26-11-08)
        ✔ constants/storefront.js: MENU_CATEGORIES, ORDER_STATUSES (shared with the controllers later) @done(26-11-08)
        ✔ MenuItem: name (unique — the seed matches on it), category, isAvailable (default true, the sold-out switch), variants [{ name, price ≥ 0 }] (≥ 1, names unique within the item; Classic S / M, Hug and toppings one "Regular"), sortOrder; no soft delete (no page deletes menu items) @done(26-11-08)
        ✔ StorefrontOrder: items 1–30 lines [{ menuItem ref, snapshot of category / name / variantName / unitPrice (a later price or name change can't rewrite placed orders; no populate needed), qty integer 1–20, separateToppings (only when category is classic) }], customerName (≤ 40), customerPhone (digits only via setter, /^0\d{8,9}$/, select: false like User.password so only .select('+customerPhone') sees it), totalPrice (must equal Σ unitPrice × qty), status (default pending_payment), queueNumber, confirmedBy (ref User), confirmedAt, readyAt, pickedUpAt, timestamps; index { status, createdAt } for the staff tabs @done(26-11-08)
        ✔ StoreSetting: _id 'storefront', isOpen (default false), updatedBy (ref User), timestamps; getStore() treats a missing document as closed (and doesn't create one) @done(26-11-08)
        ✔ Counter: { _id: 'queue-YYYY-MM-DD', seq }; nextQueueNumber(now) = one findOneAndUpdate $inc + upsert on the Thai date (Intl, Asia/Bangkok) — atomic, starts at 1 each day with no scheduled job @done(26-11-08)
        ✔ Tested on the dev DB (throwaway script, "ZZ" data, removed): 33/33 — valid saves; empty / duplicate variants, bad category, negative price, duplicate name (E11000) refused; "081-234-5678" → 0812345678, "02 123 4567" → 021234567, "12345" / "+66812345678" / missing refused; separateToppings on a topping, qty 0 / 21 / 1.5, wrong total, no items, 31 lines, 41-char name, unknown status refused; findById and its JSON have no phone, select('+customerPhone') does; status_1_createdAt_1 index built; two simultaneous nextQueueNumber → 1 and 2, then 3; getStore() → closed without writing; old collections' counts unchanged, new ones empty. Day rollover tested without the DB (Atlas refused a second connection, TLS alert): 16:59 UTC → queue-2026-11-08, 17:00 / 17:30 UTC → queue-2026-11-09 @done(26-11-08)
    ✔ 2b. Bites in the models (branch feat/storefront-bites): MENU_CATEGORIES gains 'bites' (and is now in menu order), new SEPARATE_TOPPING_CATEGORIES ['classic', 'bites'] used by the separateToppings validator, category error message built from the list. Tested with validate() (no DB needed): bites item saves; unknown category refused with all 4 listed; Bites and Classic lines may have a separate cup, Hug and topping lines may not @done(26-11-08)
    ✔ 3. Seed script scripts/seedMenu.js (branch feat/storefront-seed-menu) @done(26-11-08)
        ✔ Names (Jui 11-8-26): English, except the condensed-milk topping = "นมข้น" only; order within each category as in REQUIREMENTS. Name = what the menu row shows ("Plain"); the cart / staff pages put the category label in front ("Classic · Plain (M)") as the design does @done(26-11-08)
        ✔ MenuItem unique index changed from name to { category, name } — Classic and Hug both have Plain / Choco Pops / Choco Berry. name_1 dropped from dev by hand (Mongoose never drops indexes); production never had the collection @done(26-11-08)
        ✔ 12 items: Hug Plain 59 / Choco Pops 69 / Choco Berry 79; Classic Plain S59 M99 / Choco Pops S69 M119 / Choco Berry S89 M149 / Signature S79 M129; Strawberry Nutella Bites 129; Choc dip / Choc pops / Strawberry freeze dried / นมข้น 10. Single-variant items use "Regular"; sortOrder 1, 2, 3… per category from the list order @done(26-11-08)
        ✔ Re-run rules: creates missing items; brings variants / sortOrder back in line and prints each change (the way prices change — no menu page; edit prices.js too); never touches isAvailable (staff's sold-out switch); never deletes (unknown items only reported); store setting created closed only if missing, timestamps set by hand on insert so a re-run doesn't move "Opened at"; ENV_FILE + y/N via scriptEnv.js; touches MenuItem + StoreSetting only @done(26-11-08)
        ✔ Tested on dev: N → nothing written; run 1 created 12 + store (closed); run 2 all "up to date". Throwaway re-run test 13/13: S price 1 → 59 and reported, Choc dip order 9 → 1 and reported, a sold-out นมข้น stays sold out, an open store stays open with updatedAt unchanged, an unknown item reported not deleted, a second classic · Plain refused (E11000) while churro-hug · Plain coexists, indexes = _id_ + category_1_name_1, collection counts restored. Dev keeps the seeded menu (12 items, all available, store closed) for building the API @done(26-11-08)
    ✔ 4. Public API /api/storefront (no protect) — branch feat/storefront-public-api; storefrontController.js + storefrontRoutes.js, mounted in app.js. Error messages in English; the pages show Thai and react to status codes: 403 = closed, 409 = sold out (Jui 11-9-26) @done(26-11-09)
        ✔ GET /menu → closed: { isOpen: false }, no menu; open: { isOpen: true, items } in menu order (MENU_CATEGORIES, then sortOrder), sold-out items included with isAvailable false (the design shows them) @done(26-11-09)
        ✔ POST /orders → 403 when closed (server check); items 1–30 lines, each menuItemId checked with isObjectIdOrHexString (isValidObjectId accepts any 12-char string); one $in query; unknown → 400; variantName optional only for single-variant items (Classic must say S / M); names / categories / prices copied from the DB, separateToppings only when === true, total summed from the cast lines (model re-checks); status / queueNumber / confirmedBy / prices in the body ignored; any sold-out item → 409 { data: { soldOut: [ids] } } and no order; 201 with the public order @done(26-11-09)
        ✔ GET /orders/:id → public order (works when closed); 404 unknown, 400 malformed. Every order sent back goes through toPublicOrder — a whitelist, since select: false doesn't cover a just-created document; confirmedBy left out too @done(26-11-09)
        ✔ Tested over real HTTP on dev (throwaway script, "ZZ" orders, removed): 40/40 — closed menu / 403; open menu 12 items in the right order; valid order 201, total 267 (99×2 + 10 + 59), snapshot from the DB, no phone / confirmedBy in the response, phone stored as digits; tampered price / total / status / queueNumber / name / category ignored; "yes" isn't true; 400 for missing / non-array / empty / 31-line items, malformed / 12-char / null / unknown ids, Classic without or with a wrong variant, qty 0 / 21 / 1.5 / "abc", separate cup on Hug, bad phone, no name; sold out → 409 with the id and no order; sold-out item still on the menu; GET order while closed 200 without private fields, unknown 404, malformed 400; /api/v1/orders without a token still 401; counts, store (closed) and availability restored. npm run dev restarted itself mid-run (node --watch, nothing changed) — retested on plain node server.js @done(26-11-09)
    ✔ 5. PromptPay QR (branch feat/storefront-promptpay-qr) @done(26-11-09)
        ✔ Library (Jui 11-9-26): promptparse (generate.anyId) + qrcode 1.5, not the docs' promptpay-qr — unmaintained since 2022 and pulls qrcode 0.9 → colors "*" (sabotaged by its author in 2022); promptparse is maintained, MIT, no dependencies. npm audit: no new warnings (body-parser high + qs moderate were already on main, from Express) @done(26-11-09)
        ✔ utils/promptPay.js paymentQr(amount) → { qr (PNG data URL, 480 px), accountName, amount } or null; PROMPTPAY_ID digits only, 10 = MSISDN, 13 = NATID; PROMPTPAY_NAME (Jui 11-9-26) optional; missing / malformed ID logs and returns null instead of stopping the server (a forgotten Railway variable mustn't take the dashboard down) @done(26-11-09)
        ✔ GET /api/storefront/orders/:id adds payment only while pending_payment (nothing to scan once paid / cancelled); POST doesn't build one; config.env.example documents both variables @done(26-11-09)
        ✔ Tested with FAKE ids: util 14/14 — PNG 480 px; payload parses back with a valid CRC, tag 29/01 = 0066812345678, amount 54 = 267.00, currency 764, country TH, dynamic (01 = 12); a tampered amount fails the CRC; the image encodes exactly that payload; 13 digits → NATID; no name → null; no ID / 7 digits → null + logged. HTTP with a fake ID 8/8 (POST has no payment; GET pending has qr / amount 208 / name; no phone; cooking → no payment; menu fine) and without an ID 7/7 (payment: null, server and other routes fine, error logged). "ZZ" orders removed, the dev store left open as Jui had it, Jui's own "Jui test" order untouched @done(26-11-09)
        ✔ Switched to the shop's K SHOP QR (Jui 11-9-26: Churo Bites receives through K SHOP). Its printed QR decodes to Thai QR with no amount: PromptPay bill payment (tag 30, K SHOP biller + shop ref KB000002367061), card tags, name CHURO.BITES. A ฿1 copy (tag 01 → 12, tag 54 → 1.00, new CRC) was scanned and PAID for real by Jui — money and K SHOP notification arrived @done(26-11-09)
        ✔ Code: PROMPTPAY_MERCHANT_QR = that QR text; paymentPayload fills in each order's amount the same way; PROMPTPAY_ID only when the merchant QR isn't set; a set-but-broken merchant QR (bad CRC / no tag 30) logs and returns null — never a silent fallback to a possibly different account. Tests: merchant 15/15 (valid CRC, 01 = 12, amount, every other tag identical, PROMPTPAY_ID ignored, bad / non-QR → null, blank → falls back, neither → null); the code's ฿1 payload is identical to the paid QR; mobile tests still 14/14; HTTP with the merchant QR 10/10 (served PNG decodes to the K SHOP QR with amount 208.00 and a valid CRC) @done(26-11-09)
        ☐ Jui adds PROMPTPAY_MERCHANT_QR to server/config.env (dev) and, before opening, to Railway
    ☐ 6. Staff API /api/staff (protect on every route)
        ☐ GET / PATCH /store → { isOpen }, updatedBy from req.user
        ☐ GET /orders?status=pending_payment|cooking|ready (with phone), pending oldest first, cooking by queue number
        ☐ PATCH /orders/:id/confirm → cooking + queue number (Counter $inc) + confirmedBy / confirmedAt — status in the update filter so two phones can't confirm the same order twice
        ☐ PATCH /orders/:id/ready, /pickup, /cancel — same "only from the right status" filter
        ☐ PATCH /menu/:itemId → { isAvailable } (not /variants/:variantId as in the docs — availability is on the item, 11-8-26)
    ☐ 7. Rate limit POST /api/storefront/orders (express-rate-limit, keyed on X-Real-IP in production like login)
    ☐ 8. Test against the dev DB with throwaway scripts ("ZZ …" data, removed afterwards): closed store 403, price tampering ignored, queue numbers per day, double confirm refused, phone never in the public API

